      "text": "375 \u00d7 775 = 375 \u00d7 700 + 375 \u00d7 75.\n\\[ 375 \\times 775 = 375 \\times 700 + 375 \\times 75 \\].\n\n### Step 5: Calculate Each Part.\nLet's calculate each part separately:\n\\[ 375 \\times 700 = 375 \\times (7 \\times 100) = (375 \\times 7) \\times 100 \\].\n\\[ 375 \\times 7 = 2625 \\].\n\\[ 375 \\times 700 = 2625 \\times 100 = 262500 \\].\n\nNext, calculate:\n\\[ 375 \\times 75 = 375 \\times (7 \\times 10 + 5) = (375 \\times 7) \\times 10 + (375 \\times 5) \\].\n\\[ 375 \\times 7 = 2625 \\].\n\\[ 375 \\times 5 = 1875 \\].\n\\[ 375 \\times 75 = 2625 \\times 10 + 1875 = 26250 + 1875 = 28125 \\].\n\n### Step 6: Add the Results.\nNow, add the two results together:\n\\[ 262500 + 28125 = 290625 \\].\n\n### Final Answer:\nTherefore, the product of 375 and 775 is:\n\\[ 375 \\times 775 = 290625 \\].",
